## Why

I have selected the figure of Thomas Aquinas represented as the "Angelic Doctor" to embody the encyclical *Studiorum Ducem*. This single, recognizable subject perfectly translates the document's central theme: the inseparable bond between Aquinas's personal sanctity (signified by the angelic wings and halo) and the divine authority of his doctrine (signified by the open book and writing stylus). By choosing this iconic figure over an abstract form, the sculpture achieves immediate legibility, allowing the viewer to instantly connect the subject with the peak of Catholic theological study and holiness celebrated by Pope Pius XI. The concrete materials of marble and bronze reinforce the timeless and enduring nature of his teachings as the foundation of Catholic education.

